          <button class="faq-question">What is the absolute cheapest way to insure a car? <span>+</span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            Carry state minimum liability on a paid-off older car (skipping collision and comprehensive), then stack telematics, paperless auto-pay, and a renters or homeowners bundle. Just make sure you have enough liability coverage to protect your savings if you cause a serious crash.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question">Why did my car insurance rate go up if I had no accidents? <span>+</span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            Insurers periodically get state approval to raise base rates across an entire ZIP code when local repair costs, medical bills, hailstorms, or injury lawsuits climb. Some carriers also nudge renewal prices up on loyal customers who rarely shop around, which is why comparing quotes once a year pays off.
